Oz: every player on the board, up to 64. A server command holds 1022 characters, about 25 players of
id's "scores", and id's game cut the list there (ioquake3's at 1000 characters). Oz's game sends the rest
first as "scoresmore <first> <count> ...", then "scores" with the first part as id's game sends it; the cgame
keeps the parts until "scores" comes and puts them together, as the engine's HUD does. The game's memory pool
held about 26 bots (a bot's state is 8.8 KB of its 256 KB): it holds 1 MB, so 63 bots fill a 64-player server.

